import EthInapproximability.CurrentPaper.WeightedVertexWord
import EthInapproximability.CurrentPaper.WeightedRowFieldsSpec
import EthInapproximability.CurrentPaper.WeightedLevelFields15

/-! Lane owner:b-weighted-level-3, unit 2, segment 1 (2c-ii), third piece
(GENERATED by gen_level0rows.py): the level-0 composite on ONE combined bank.

`CStack = WeightedScalarComplete.Stack ⊕ (Fin 7 ⊕ WeightedRawWords.Aux)`: the
consumer/writer region shared by the raw-words machine and the frozen level
controller, the level controller's retained `save` region, and the raw-words
master region. ONE fixed program, four phases joined by charged handoffs
(`BitMachineRawSequence.runs`), each embedded by `WeightedRawWords.region_run`
(production `BitMachineStackRun.run`):
1. `WeightedVertexWord.rawWordsKVProgram M c` (frozen raw-words program with the
   k fuel, then the retained `|VG|` word);
2. the frozen, accepted owner-2 controller `WeightedLevelFields15.program` at
   level 0 (`y = y₀`, `lvl = 0`, `M = seedMatrix b`), started on the bank the
   raw words produced (same-object: `runParameters … 0 = stepParameters …`);
3. a charged pop clear of the reached writer cells 7, 18, 47..53 (their lengths
   bounded through the admitted `BitMachineStackGrowth.run_growth`);
4. the row-field program (`WeightedRowFields.rowProgram`) with inputs writer
   9/15/16/17/29/21/1 and the master `|VG|` cell, outputs writer 7, 18, 47..53
   and two master cells for the protected writer's `rows`/`cols` words, scratch
   in master `nat 3 _` cells (cleared).
The exit bank is an exact function of the named existential scalar scratch
banks `F, Q, P` of the frozen level controller. -/

namespace EthInapproximability.CurrentPaper.WeightedLevel0Rows

open Turing BitMachineEncoding BitMachineStackEmbedding
open EthInapproximability.ParameterizedNP.GuardedSourceGraph

